# fixed-constants-over-contextual-estimation

Operational planning pipelines that consume finite, countable resources must use pre-agreed, fixed consumption constants rather than context-sensitive estimates, creative reductions, or per-cycle improvisations. Fixed constants ensure auditability, prevent shortfall masking, and make consumption predictable and comparable across planning cycles.

## Procedures
- Establish and document fixed consumption rates per resource type before any plan is generated.
- Apply those constants uniformly — never adjust them based on available supply or time pressure.
- Validate that available inventory meets the full fixed-rate requirement before producing a plan.
- If the fixed rate cannot be met by available supply, halt — do not silently reduce the rate to fit.

